# Performance & scalability (Global)

- Don’t micro-optimize by default; do flag obvious foot-guns:
  - N+1 queries, unbounded loops, loading large datasets/files into memory.
- Data access: prefer pagination/batching/filtering; avoid `SELECT *` on large tables.
- External calls: include timeouts; retries must be bounded and consider idempotency.
- Add caching only when it’s justified and consistent with the repo; avoid new infra deps unless asked.
